# THE GRAPH — SAVIOURS RULE

OFFICIAL SOURCES

The Graph:
https://thegraph.com/docs/

Standardized Subgraphs:
https://thegraph.com/docs/en/subgraphs/existing-subgraphs/standard-subgraphs/

Subgraph MCP:
https://thegraph.com/docs/en/subgraphs/tooling/subgraph-mcp/introduction/

Agent0 / ERC-8004:
https://thegraph.com/docs/en/subgraphs/existing-subgraphs/agent0/

Subgraph Skills:
https://github.com/graphprotocol/subgraphs-skills

Substreams:
https://github.com/streamingfast/substreams-skills

MANDATORY DOCUMENTATION WORKFLOW

Before implementing Graph functionality:

1. Inspect existing Graph code.
2. Identify the exact Graph product being used.
3. Consult the current official documentation.
4. Verify the current schema/API/network support.
5. Check whether a standardized or composable product already provides
   the requirement.
6. Only then implement.

NEVER GUESS

Do not invent:
- GraphQL entity names
- GraphQL field names
- query structure
- endpoints
- deployment IDs
- network identifiers
- API behavior
- MCP tools
- SDK methods

LOAD-BEARING REQUIREMENT

The Graph is an intelligence/evidence layer.

Graph data must influence:
- investigation
- reasoning
- risk assessment
- decisions
- recommendations
- monitoring
- automation
- transaction policy

Do not build:
User → Graph query → display raw result

PREFERRED PATH

Standardized Subgraphs
→ Composable Graph products
→ Subgraph MCP
→ Substreams
→ custom subgraph only when justified

COMPOSABLE / STANDARDIZED REQUIREMENT

Whenever possible demonstrate:

ONE QUERY PATTERN
→ MULTIPLE PROTOCOLS
→ NORMALIZED DATA
→ AI REASONING
→ SECURITY DECISION

If targeting the Composable/Standardized Graph prize, the implementation
must make the standards leverage demonstrable, e.g.:

"One investigation interface can query protocol-standardized data
without requiring protocol-specific query logic."

LIVE DATA

Real product paths must consume live Graph-provider data.

Do not use:
- mocked Graph responses
- static blockchain datasets
- fake activity
- hardcoded analytics

Fixtures are allowed only under /evals.

SECURITY BOUNDARY

Graph indexed data is not automatically the final source of truth for
security-critical authorization.

When necessary:

Graph evidence
→ direct onchain verification
→ deterministic policy
→ transaction authorization

ARCHITECTURE

Keep Graph queries isolated from:
- UI
- AI reasoning
- transaction execution

Graph adapters return normalized Evidence objects.

Before coding, report:

### Graph documentation consulted
### Graph product used
### Schema/API verified
### Standardization/composition opportunity
### Why Graph is load-bearing
### Implementation plan
